<B>INQUERY STOPWORD LIST FOR THOMAS</B>=20
<HR>

<P>Stopwords are those words which are judged to be so common in an =
online=20
system that they have little information value. Thus, in order to =
enhance system=20
performance for the online searcher, stopwords are not indexed, and =
therefore=20
<EM><B>are not searchable</B></EM>. In practical terms, this means that =
the=20
THOMAS searcher would not get any results back from a search on a phrase =
such as=20
"<EM>to be or not to be</EM>," since each of those words is a stopword =
in=20
THOMAS.=20
<P>The stopword list used by the InQuery search system in THOMAS =
comprises the=20
following words:=20
<HR>

